From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 06:48:27 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] generate_qmap: map MediaTek's programmable key

MediaTek's keypad driver takes its keymap from the vendor's device tree,
and on the Unihertz Titan that map gives the red programmable key on the
left side the keycode 250. Linux has no name for 250, and neither Qt's
default table nor this one has an entry for it, so the evdev handler drops
the key before any Qt key event exists and Settings > Buttons cannot offer
it however the device is configured.

It is what KEY_PROG1 is on other phones, so it gets KEY_PROG1's Qt key,
Key_Launch1. A phone that had both would see them as one key; none of the
supported phones does.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 tools/generate_qmap/webos_keymap_p.h | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/tools/generate_qmap/webos_keymap_p.h
+++ b/tools/generate_qmap/webos_keymap_p.h
@@ -46,7 +46,13 @@ const QEvdevKeyboardMap::Mapping webos_keymap[] = {
     { 112, 0xffff, Qt::Key_Launch2,     0x00, 0x00, 0x0000 }, // KEY_MACRO
     { 148, 0xffff, Qt::Key_Launch1,     0x00, 0x00, 0x0000 }, // KEY_PROG1
     { 212, 0xffff, Qt::Key_Camera,      0x00, 0x00, 0x0000 }, // KEY_CAMERA
-    { 528, 0xffff, Qt::Key_CameraFocus, 0x00, 0x00, 0x0000 }  // KEY_CAMERA_FOCUS
+    { 528, 0xffff, Qt::Key_CameraFocus, 0x00, 0x00, 0x0000 }, // KEY_CAMERA_FOCUS
+
+    // MediaTek's keypad driver reports the programmable key of a phone such
+    // as the Unihertz Titan as 250, a code with no name in Linux, from the
+    // vendor's device tree. It is the same key KEY_PROG1 is on other phones,
+    // so it gets the same Qt key.
+    { 250, 0xffff, Qt::Key_Launch1,     0x00, 0x00, 0x0000 }  // MediaTek programmable key
 };
 
 #endif // WEBOS_KEYMAP_P_H
